    <item>
      <title>'My life and this world will never be the same without you' - Tributes paid to Hampshire gamekeeper</title>
      <link>https://www.farmersguardian.com/news/4522811/life-world-tributes-paid-hampshire-gamekeeper</link>
      <description>A fundraiser has been created to commemorate a 'hard-working, kind and generous' gamekeeper who died last month. Tributes have flooded in to remember Tony Rietzler, from Chawton near Alton, who died on November 12. LISTEN NOW: The fundraiser said the 26-year-old died in a road traffic collision. Mr Rietzler worked as a gamekeeper in Marlborough and at Wellers Place Farm in Bentworth. He studied Game and Wildlife Management at Sparsholt College. Lily English, a family friend, launched a GoFundMe</description>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.farmersguardian.com/news/4522811/life-world-tributes-paid-hampshire-gamekeeper</guid>
